@startuml
' THE CHAIN OF LOGIC — how one extracted artifact becomes (or fails to become) a claim.
' This is the diagram that matters: every guard here exists because skipping it produces a
' confident, wrong answer. Re-render: plantuml -tsvg -tpng docs/diagrams/*.puml
!include _theme.puml
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 12

start
:**Artifact extracted**
<size:11>favicon · tracker ID · TLS cert · JARM · wallet</size>
<size:11>registrant · signing cert · URL-path kit · doc metadata</size>;

if (**Base-rate it.** How many\nunrelated hosts carry this\nexact value?) then (**many**)
  :**Convention, not campaign.**
  Parked-page favicon, managed NS,
  `/login`, a bundler filename,
  a provider default banner.
  <size:11>Recorded as a FACT. Never an edge.</size>; <<#FBF0EF>>
  stop
else (**few**)
endif

if (On a **noise denylist**?\n<size:11>registrar / privacy proxy / CDN range /</size>\n<size:11>generic label / role placeholder</size>) then (**yes**)
  :**Shared infrastructure.**
  It names other *customers*,
  not an operator.
  <size:11>Lead only — never auto-seeded.</size>; <<#FBF0EF>>
  stop
else (**no**)
endif

:**Becomes a KB node**
<size:11>the host that carried it links to it</size>;

if (How many **independent**\nartifact CLASSES do the\nhosts share?) then (**one**)
  :**LEAD.**
  A single shared node is a
  lead, never proof.
  <size:11>→ collect more, or say so out loud</size>; <<#FDF8EC>>
  stop
else (**two or more**)
endif

if (Is the shared thing the\n**operator's**, or the **kit's**?) then (kit / platform)
  :**SAME-KIT.**
  Shared template, white-label
  platform, purchased kit,
  malware family, path directory.
  <size:11>Two resellers look identical here.</size>; <<#FDF8EC>>
  stop
else (operator-controlled)
endif

:**SAME-OPERATOR**
<size:11>account tokens · registrant · payout wallet</size>
<size:11>origin IP with overlapping hosting window</size>;

if (**Temporal check** — did the\nshared value overlap in TIME?) then (no overlap)
  :**Sequential tenancy.**
  Same value, different eras =
  two owners, not one.; <<#FDF8EC>>
  stop
else (overlaps)
endif

:**Adversarially verify**
<size:11>try HARD to refute the link before committing it</size>;

if (Survived?) then (**no**)
  :**Rejected.**
  Record the rejection —
  a tested-and-dropped link is
  worth as much as a kept one.; <<#FBF0EF>>
  stop
else (**yes**)
endif

:**Attributed claim + calibrated confidence**
<size:11>ICD-203 estimative language · every dated fact cited</size>
<size:11>to an ONLINE source, never a cases/ path</size>; <<#F0F8F7>>
stop
@enduml
